  "limitations": [
    "Rust assignment into an existing slot drops the old Rust value and moves the cloned temporary. It cannot reproduce arbitrary user-defined C++ move-assignment/destructor hook side effects.",
    "The safe borrowed API does not expose native source/key self-aliasing. Allocation-before-copy and key-copy failure cleanup are covered for the Rust node owner, but Rust panic behavior and native exception classes/subobject side effects are not interchangeable.",
    "Rust represents the entry as an allocator-owned Entry rather than OCCT\u2019s combined list node, while bucket-table storage follows a different allocator path."
  ],
